# unknown tag
board/urls.go:34:40: unknown key "mim" in the tag of form field Title
  fix: did you mean "min"? allowed: label, help, choices, min, max, min_value, max_value, optional

# not a Field
board/urls.go:36:9: form field Rate is float64, not maago.Field[T]
  fix: use maago.Field[T] with T one of string, int64, int32, float64, bool, time.Time; a file field comes with M7

# a type forms do not read
board/urls.go:36:9: form field Rate is maago.Field[uint8], not maago.Field[T]
  fix: use maago.Field[T] with T one of string, int64, int32, float64, bool, time.Time; a file field comes with M7

# unexported
board/urls.go:36:2: form field rate is not exported
  fix: export it: templates draw the form's fields

# min on a number
board/urls.go:35:40: min applies to strings, but form field Days is int32
  fix: use min_value=…: min and max count the characters of a string

# min_value on a string
board/urls.go:34:40: min_value applies to numbers, but form field Title is string
  fix: remove it; min and max bound a string's length

# a value past the type
board/urls.go:35:62: max_value of form field Days is "3000000000", not a int32
  fix: write a number of the field's type

# min above max
board/urls.go:34:2: form field Title has min=300 above max=200
  fix: swap them

# optional checkbox
board/urls.go:37:35: form field Pinned is a checkbox, which is never required
  fix: remove optional

# choices on a number
board/urls.go:35:40: choices apply to strings, but form field Days is int32
  fix: remove choices, or make the field a string

# no such model
board/urls.go:27:27: form BoardForm names model Bord, which this package does not declare
  fix: did you mean "Board"?

# no such model field
board/urls.go:28:2: model Board has no field Nam
  fix: did you mean "Name"?

# a model form's own rule
board/urls.go:29:41: form field Kind takes its rules from model Board
  fix: remove max; a model form's field may only add optional, and model Board declares the rest

# model type differs
board/urls.go:28:13: form field Name is maago.Field[int64], but model Board has it as string
  fix: make it maago.Field[string]

# auto in a model form
board/urls.go:29:2: field Created of model Board is not for a form to set
  fix: remove it; the database or the generated code sets it

# two forms in an In
board/urls.go:45:2: BoardIn reads a second form, More
  fix: keep one form field in In; a page with two forms posts each to its own route

# not a form
board/urls.go:52:2: NoticeIn.Form reads form NoticePage, which does not embed maago.Form
  fix: embed maago.Form in NoticePage, and make its fields maago.Field[T]

# another package's form
board/urls.go:52:7: form Form is not of a type of this package: time.Time
  fix: declare the form struct in this package, embedding maago.Form

# form with a value
board/urls.go:52:26: maago:"form" takes no value
  fix: write maago:"form"; the form's keys are its fields' names

# a typo before model
board/urls.go:27:21: unknown key "foo" in the tag of maago.Form
  fix: the form's own tag takes model=X: maago:"model=Board"
board/urls.go:27:31: form BoardForm names model Bord, which this package does not declare
  fix: did you mean "Board"?

# ID in a model form
board/urls.go:29:2: field ID of model Board is not for a form to set
  fix: remove it; the database or the generated code sets it

# a form on DELETE
board/urls.go:52:2: NoticeIn.Form reads a form, but route notice_create is a DELETE, which names what it removes in its path
  fix: send the form with POST; DELETE takes its values from the path

# a form on a GET API route
board/urls.go:52:2: NoticeIn.Form reads a form, but API route api_notice_create is a GET, which sends no body
  fix: read the values with query= fields, or make the route a POST

# a generated name taken
board/urls.go:54:2: form NoticeForm would declare invalidNoticeForm, which board/urls.go:43 declares already
  fix: rename what else declares invalidNoticeForm

# a pointer form
board/urls.go:52:7: form Form is a pointer
  fix: declare it as NoticeForm; the adapter fills it in place

# Validate on the value
board/urls.go:41:21: Validate of form NoticeForm has a value receiver: the errors it sets are lost
  fix: declare it func (f *NoticeForm) Validate()

# two forms at once
board/urls.go:27:27: form BoardForm names model Bord, which this package does not declare
  fix: did you mean "Board"?
board/urls.go:34:40: unknown key "mim" in the tag of form field Title
  fix: did you mean "min"? allowed: label, help, choices, min, max, min_value, max_value, optional

# Validate's signature
board/urls.go:41:22: Validate of form NoticeForm is not a method func()
  fix: declare func (f *NoticeForm) Validate(): it sets a field's Error or calls f.AddError; a check that needs the database goes in the view (D-119)

